    <section class="use-cases-grid" aria-label="Duo Input details">
        <article class="use-cases-panel">
            <h2 data-section-label="Business impact">What changes for the business</h2>
            <details open>
                <summary>Staff and customers can work at the same time</summary>
                <p>A representative can keep processing the case while the customer enters information, confirms details or signs on the second screen.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Fewer interruptions in the flow</summary>
                <p>Customer touch input no longer has to take over the same active cursor that staff are using, which helps keep service moments calm and predictable.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>A smoother two-screen experience</summary>
                <p>The business can offer shared progress visibility while each person interacts with the part of the workflow meant for them.</p>
            </details>
        </article>

        <article class="use-cases-panel">
            <h2 data-section-label="Use cases">Where it helps</h2>
            <details open>
                <summary>Customer-facing counters and service desks</summary>
                <p>Use one system across two displays when staff need to continue working while the customer interacts on a dedicated customer screen.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Forms and data entry</summary>
                <p>Let customers enter details such as email, phone number or consent while the staff side remains usable.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Digital signatures</summary>
                <p>Capture a signature on the customer display while the service screen keeps the name, context and workflow visible.</p>
            </details>
        </article>

        <article class="use-cases-panel">
            <h2 data-section-label="Value">Why it matters</h2>
            <details open>
                <summary>Better service without extra handoffs</summary>
                <p>Both users can stay in the same flow instead of waiting for control to move back and forth between displays.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Less custom workaround work</summary>
                <p>Duo Input solves the input problem below the application layer, so teams can improve the interaction model without rebuilding every screen from scratch.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Designed for real operating environments</summary>
                <p>The product is intended for shared systems where two people need reliable input at the same time.</p>
            </details>
        </article>

        <article class="use-cases-panel">
